{"event_type":"review","id":"107e69299cdec214b696629189ac45ffcc1931d2487d20f5a2ca67d5402989f9","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T22:29:54Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0159b965cff48baa0d6f07ef78b89e89906afca5453b40a066b9a90faf7a1103","sha256":"0159b965cff48baa0d6f07ef78b89e89906afca5453b40a066b9a90faf7a1103"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d5d6da196864cc9bbe183b1f63aee19dc53050e6159e3e75c754ac0bdffd55c2","sha256":"d5d6da196864cc9bbe183b1f63aee19dc53050e6159e3e75c754ac0bdffd55c2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e4f4902f43ec9ad5ec4d8200bb689f9064ad2cb9ecd296c31188b3ffce8e415f","sha256":"e4f4902f43ec9ad5ec4d8200bb689f9064ad2cb9ecd296c31188b3ffce8e415f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/396a35261205dc2991608854857500c9a45c8f3c058ef546287a55df9295e744","sha256":"396a35261205dc2991608854857500c9a45c8f3c058ef546287a55df9295e744"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f8436d954945aff36568c7f91fab6b1bac7d1404d882598ebae995a2f843da95","sha256":"f8436d954945aff36568c7f91fab6b1bac7d1404d882598ebae995a2f843da95"}],"attempt_id":"f1c675caca87b53fc03e5f093172dbf01c7d09329dab7081f8368c106c0f4714:0:1","base":"a1615fbd68dc67719aa95bcc8bb642cfca21be98","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"6feb1c2b9c09bd5a3dfc03a819bfec1b3f08b358","body":"**Check `unsafeRefusal` before `scanFailedAttempt` runs.**\n\nWhen `pushFailed` is set, `scanFailedAttempt` (Line 667) runs before the `unsafeRefusal` check (Line 676). An attempt that failed the `tamper` gate in `validateFix` is already escalated and never pushed (Line 697). The scan still runs `hackDetector` on the same patch and throws `failed-attempt tamper gate refused publication`. The catch at Line 705-715 then sets `indeterminate` and runs `break taskLoop`.\n\nThe result:\n- The loop marks every remaining task `unit stopped for human review` (Line 729-737).\n- `pushBranch` is skipped because `indeterminate` is set (Line 742). Verified commits from earlier tasks stay local.\n\nWith `pushFailed: false`, the same tamper-gate failure only ends that task, and the unit still publishes its verified commits. Turning on the opt-in therefore stops verified fixes from being published, although this failed attempt was never going to be pushed.\n\nSkip the scan when the attempt will not be published anyway:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (config.pushFailed && row.failedAttempt !== undefined) {\n+          const unsafeRefusal = row.validation?.gates.some(\n+            (gate) =>\n+              ['paths', 'tamper', 'commit'].includes(gate.gate) && gate.verdict !== 'pass',\n+          );\n+          if (!unsafeRefusal) {\n           try {\n             const uploadGate = await scanFailedAttempt(\n               git,\n               bindings,\n               parent,\n               row.failedAttempt.sha,\n               config.protectTests ?? false,\n             );\n             if (bindings.cancelled?.() || currentJobContext()?.signal.aborted)\n               throw new Error('parent job cancelled before failed-attempt publication');\n-            const unsafeRefusal = row.validation?.gates.some(\n-              (gate) =>\n-                ['paths', 'tamper', 'commit'].includes(gate.gate) && gate.verdict !== 'pass',\n-            );\n             if (uploadGate.kind !== 'clean') {\n               ...\n-            } else if (!unsafeRefusal) {\n+            } else {\n               await git([...push...]);\n               row.failedAttemptPublished = true;\n             }\n           } catch (publishError) {\n             ...\n           }\n+          }\n         }\n```\n</details>\n\nRecovery is possible on a rerun through `pendingPublish`, so I rated this minor.","id":"f04231d3e82c2f894a087485301d4251a3cf93d2e8022df91a593ac07cb60f53","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/sweep/taskLoop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check `unsafeRefusal` before `scanFailedAttempt` runs."}],"head":"4aca517b8f44e176885b7d60457cc3b75d522cc3","head_tree":"74119e2e60617e97b4070712a18195b8b48c1179","input_scope":[{"blob":"890d959ff15cc4b476ae6549ac322016f60eacc1","intervals":[[9,9],[12,12],[37,37],[44,55],[65,80],[95,156],[176,186],[193,197],[199,236],[244,279],[292,300],[342,343],[368,368],[443,443],[528,545],[577,583],[600,625],[638,642],[653,725],[751,784],[791,791],[805,821]],"path":"src/ops/fix/runFix.ts"},{"blob":"6feb1c2b9c09bd5a3dfc03a819bfec1b3f08b358","intervals":[[3,3],[7,7],[13,13],[27,28],[36,36],[58,59],[65,67],[70,102],[261,263],[265,266],[268,268],[270,297],[321,325],[329,329],[335,335],[385,391],[395,399],[453,453],[479,479],[511,522],[546,564],[625,630],[638,641],[648,658],[660,660],[665,716],[781,781],[783,1021]],"path":"src/ops/sweep/taskLoop.ts"},{"blob":"61f15fd0e94ab5f8693bc5756dd03de11e95637b","intervals":[[1,6],[11,100],[127,610]],"path":"test/ops/fix/runFix.test.ts"},{"blob":"9381f6750c3f4acd1d854c1d9329cb72461c3863","intervals":[[2,2],[8,8],[11,12],[25,79],[85,85],[91,138],[140,141],[144,201],[203,203],[205,801]],"path":"test/ops/sweep/task-evidence.test.ts"},{"blob":"da4e6971b9f84813c49bc41f1b53e37587525eea","intervals":[[119,120],[202,207],[211,414],[709,1061],[1070,1071],[1099,1099],[1271,1272],[1675,1787]],"path":"test/ops/sweep/unit-scenarios.test.ts"}],"job_id":"f1c675caca87b53fc03e5f093172dbf01c7d09329dab7081f8368c106c0f4714:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"defd21b27682a84f6c13cf784d08db1f1a57a818","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/fix/runFix.ts"},"merge":"f83d18f3ccb74320a94d347c106208d0aa030c10","method":"pre-merge","pre":"c526e232992edb0bafd9fbba5a40a46a9f7f5219","source_path":"src/ops/fix/runFix.ts"},"blob":"890d959ff15cc4b476a